---
intent: >
  Update aide_info's response shape and tests to match the four-state brain
  vocabulary (`ok`, `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`). The tool is
  a passive forwarder of `buildBrainState(root)`; the orchestrator code
  itself stays a verbatim forward. The work is concentrated in test fixtures
  and assertions: drop every reference to the retired `invalid-path` state
  and the retired `rootPath` field, replace `connector` with `name`, and
  verify the four-state vocabulary surfaces unchanged through the tool.
---

## Project Structure

```
src/tools/info/
├── .aide               ← [unchanged] spec was rewritten to the four-state contract
├── plan.aide           ← [this file]
├── todo.aide           ← [unchanged] historical alignment trail
├── index.ts            ← [verify, edit only if drift] passive forwarder
│                          signature unchanged: default async function
│                            info(root: string): Promise<InfoResult>
│                          composes { serverVersion, outdated, brain } where
│                          `brain` is the verbatim BrainState from
│                          `buildBrainState(root)` — no transformation.
└── index.test.ts       ← [rewrite test fixtures + cases] update fixtures
                          to the four-state vocabulary; drop invalid-path
                          fixtures and assertions; replace `connector` with
                          `name`; drop `rootPath` from fixture shapes;
                          assert `name` is forwarded into result.brain on
                          states that carry it.
```

The orchestrator file (`index.ts`) does not need behavioral changes — it
already forwards `buildBrainState`'s output verbatim into `result.brain`.
Once the prerequisite plan lands and the `BrainState` type is the
four-variant union with `name` instead of `connector` and no `rootPath`,
the orchestrator's existing forward picks up the new shape automatically.
This plan exists to (a) verify the orchestrator stays a verbatim forward
under the new shape, (b) refresh the test fixtures and assertions to the
new vocabulary so the suite continues to enforce the contract.

## Prerequisites

**`src/service/buildBrainState/`** must complete its rewrite to the new
four-state contract before this plan runs.

The contract this plan consumes:

- `BrainState` in `@/types/index.js` is a four-variant tagged union:
  `ok`, `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`. No `invalid-path`
  variant.
- `BrainState` carries no `rootPath` field on any variant. It carries no
  `connector` field. The `ok`, `no-mcp-entry`, and `mcp-drift` variants
  carry `name: string` (the user-declared descriptive label from
  brain.aide). The `no-brain-aide` variant carries only `hints`. Every
  variant carries `hints: BrainHint[]`.
- `buildBrainState(root: string): Promise<BrainState>` returns one of
  these four variants and never throws.

The implementor of this plan will hit TypeScript errors in
`src/tools/info/index.test.ts` if the prerequisite has not landed —
specifically, the existing test fixtures reference `rootPath`, `connector`,
and the `invalid-path` status, none of which exist in the new union. That
is the expected signal to wait for the prerequisite. No coordination
work in this plan beyond declaring the dependency.

## Plan

### 1. Verify `index.ts` is a verbatim forward under the new shape

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/data-flow`

- [x] 1a. Open `src/tools/info/index.ts` and confirm the orchestrator
      already forwards `buildBrainState(root)`'s return value unchanged
      into the `brain` field of the returned `InfoResult`. The expected
      shape — already in place — is:
      - `serverVersion: readServerVersion()` (sync read of bundled
        `package.json`).
      - `outdated: await resolveOutdated(root)` (existing helper that
        reads `.aide/versions.json` and compares against canonical).
      - `brain: await buildBrainState(root)` (verbatim forward).
      - The two async reads run in parallel via `Promise.all`.
- [x] 1b. If the orchestrator does ANY transformation of `brain` between
      receiving it from `buildBrainState` and returning it (field
      stripping, field rewrite, compatibility shim, defaulting,
      shape massaging), strip that code. The contract is verbatim
      forward — the consumer of `aide_info` reads the same plain-data
      `BrainState` the detector returned. If no transformation exists
      (the expected state), this sub-step is a no-op.
- [x] 1c. Update the orchestrator's JSDoc summary if it still references
      the five-state vocabulary or the retired `invalid-path` state.
      The current JSDoc (lines 29-47) reads "the orchestrator must halt
      and direct the user to run `/aide` when `brain.status` is anything
      other than `"ok"`" — that statement is correct under the new
      vocabulary and may stay. Any prose that enumerates specific states
      must enumerate the four current states only.
- [x] 1d. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` after the verify-edits land. The
      orchestrator must compile cleanly against the new `BrainState`
      union from the prerequisite plan. If it does not, the
      orchestrator is doing more than forwarding and must be reduced
      until it does.

