      lines 40-77 currently declares five `BrainState` constants
      (`BRAIN_OK`, `BRAIN_NO_BRAIN_AIDE`, `BRAIN_INVALID_PATH`,
      `BRAIN_NO_MCP_ENTRY`, `BRAIN_MCP_DRIFT`). Rewrite them to match
      the new four-variant union:
      - `BRAIN_OK`: `{ status: "ok", name: "obsidian", hints: [] }`.
        No `rootPath`. No `connector`. The label field is `name`.
      - `BRAIN_NO_BRAIN_AIDE`: `{ status: "no-brain-aide", hints: [] }`.
        No `name`, no path — without a usable brain.aide there is no
        descriptive label to thread through.
      - `BRAIN_NO_MCP_ENTRY`: `{ status: "no-mcp-entry", name: "obsidian",
        hints: [] }`. No `rootPath`. The `name` is from brain.aide so the
        orchestrator can name the wired brand in remediation prose.
      - `BRAIN_MCP_DRIFT`: `{ status: "mcp-drift", name: "obsidian",
        hints: [] }`. Same shape as `no-mcp-entry`.
      - **Delete `BRAIN_INVALID_PATH` entirely.** The state is retired.
- [x] 2b. Use `"obsidian"` as the canonical fixture `name` value to
      mirror the example responses in the spec body (`.aide` lines
      210-274). It is descriptive metadata only — the package never
      branches on this value.
- [x] 2c. Confirm fixtures type-check against `BrainState` from
      `@/types/index.js` (run `npx tsc --noEmit`). Each fixture is
      annotated `: BrainState` already; if the prerequisite plan has
      landed correctly, these constants compile cleanly. If not, the
