### 4. Add `name` forwarding assertions

Read: `coding-playbook/workflow/testing`

- [x] 4a. Add a new `describe("info — name field forwarding", ...)`
      block. The block contains three test cases, one per variant
      that carries `name` (`ok`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`). Each
      case mocks `buildBrainState` to return the corresponding
      fixture and asserts `expect(result.brain).toHaveProperty("name",
      "obsidian")`. This is the load-bearing test for the new
      contract: the orchestrator's verbatim forward must carry the
      user's descriptive label through to the response so the
      orchestrator can compose targeted remediation prose ("your
      Obsidian brain is wired but ...").
- [x] 4b. Add one negative case in the same block: a test that mocks
      `buildBrainState` to return `BRAIN_NO_BRAIN_AIDE` and asserts
      `expect(result.brain).not.toHaveProperty("name")`. The
      `no-brain-aide` variant carries no `name` because there is no
      usable brain.aide to read it from; verifying its absence
      prevents a regression where the forwarder defaults to a
      placeholder.

